WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.670 align:start position:0%
 
we are learning more about the inner  workings of facebook as revealed in a  massive trove of leaked documents cbs  news along with other outlets reviewed  thousands of pages of internal research  employee comments and presentations and  altogether they suggest that facebook  knew its platforms facebook instagram  whatsapp can fuel hate polarization  conspiracy theories and misinformation  but at times did little to stop it 60  minutes plus correspondent lori siegel  is here with the story lori good morning  to you they went through a lot of  documents here what'd you learn  good morning guys and facebook  whistleblower francis haugen left the  company earlier this year after  photographing thousands of pages of  documents the wall street journal first  reported on some of them and now  redacted copies have been shared by a  congressional source with journalists  around the world while the company says  there's no way to draw fair conclusions  from the quote curated selection we sat  down with one former executive who says  the documents reflect his own experience  from what was going on inside facebook  i became convinced that facebook was  causing harm in the world and causing  division in the world brian bolen spent  11 years building facebook most recently  overseeing market and product strategy  he left last year when he says he saw  the platform driving racism after george  floyd's death if i couldn't change it  and i tried and i couldn't change it and  that i couldn't be a part of it you  believe that it was tearing us apart  yeah and i'm concerned that facebook  causes divisions in a lot of areas  political being one of them and a  powerful one that we feel viscerally but  also in race and ethnicity religion  evidence of those concerns can be found  across the thousands of pages of leaked  internal records from inside the company  they provide an intimate window into  facebook's own research and the  frustrations of employees who were  trying to clean up the site we shared  some of them with bowlin these people  are phd level researchers creating  documents that are highlighting real  harms on the platform like this research  that reveals the company new vaccine  hesitancy was rampant in comments this  analysis found facebook systems missed  most of the hate speech on the platform  in afghanistan detecting it at a  worryingly low rate and this one from  july 2019 called carroll's journey into  q anon charts how a dummy account could  be served up conspiracy theories in just  two days some of this research showed  that within a week of someone just  liking a conservative account like  melania trump or donald trump they were  served up q anon content when i saw a  lot of this stuff it was enough for me  to leave the company there wasn't enough  focus on taking a research study like  that and saying shouldn't we invest a  lot of time and effort in really  understanding that the report  recommended facebook's stopped  suggesting q on content to users but it  wasn't until more than a year later that  the company banned the group it seemed  like oftentimes these changes weren't  implemented  why not because those types of safety  things are not the top priority the top  priority's growth it's the same  allegation frances haugen made when she  revealed her identity on 60 minutes  earlier this month facebook over and  over again has shown it uses profit over  safety and a claim facebook ceo mark  zuckerberg denied  writing in a post two days later this  idea we prioritize profit over safety  and well-being that's just not true but  according to one memo from last year  zuckerberg told employees they would not  move ahead with part of this proposal to  reduce bad content if the changes led to  a material trade-off in meaningful  social interactions facebook's term for  user engagement mark chose to stick with  the growth side of the business it's a  stark example of a trade-off between do  you want to reduce harmful content do  you want to reduce people's time on the  platform you choose keeping people's  time on the platform a resignation  letter posted last year from a rank and  file employee says the cold shoulder  from top management was demoralizing  integrity teams are facing increasing  barriers to building safeguards we were  willing to act only after things had  spiraled into a dire state do you think  that this is a fair characterization  it's a very fair characterization if you  look at the history of facebook they  clean up the mess after the fact  [Applause]  and there may have been no bigger mess  than the january 6 attack on the u.s  capitol according to this document  safety measures put in place ahead of  the election were rolled back and only  reintroduced after the riot broke out  internally frustration boiled over one  employee wrote haven't we had enough  time to figure out how to manage  discourse without enabling violence it  felt like the people who were closest to  understanding the work and closest to  understanding the problem were the ones  most frustrated in a statement a  facebook spokesperson told cbs news the  leaked pages lack context and leave an  incomplete distorted picture of our  company there's this very strong story  being told that these documents are  cherry-picked and i can tell you as  somebody who's been there that's just  not true you are part of these products  you helped build these products you  probably made millions why should we  listen to you i don't benefit from  speaking up negatively against former  friends and co-workers there are real  harms being caused to real human beings  and at the end of the day you can decide  whether you want to listen to me or you  can look at a bunch of documents that  were written by some of the most  talented people in the world that are  saying the same things virtual reality  bolan is sounding the alarm as the  company is pouring millions into an  ambitious plan to move beyond social  media and develop its own virtual world  a facebook metaverse we're entering a  new era of the web it's in these virtual  worlds where our children will live and  they will have their identities should  we trust the company no you shouldn't  and you should be terrified because if  the company is going to build a new  metaverse but is going to have safety  security protecting against  misinformation and hate speech  is a relatively low priority what world  is that going to be  facebook says it's invested millions in  developing these new products  responsibly the company declined to make  ceo mark zuckerberg available for an  interview but said in a statement we're  a business and we make profit but the  idea that we do so at the expense of  people's safety or well-being  misunderstands where our own commercial  interests lie  these facebook papers are now part of  several whistle whistleblower complaints  francis haugen filed with federal  officials such an interesting bit of  reporting there facebook saying oh these  are cherry-picked and the whistleblowers  are saying oh it's a whole field of  cherries it's nothing but cherries right  pick anyone uh brian boland uh the  executive who came forward to you he's  criticizing the company does he have a  prescription for fixing things  yeah i mean i think that's important he  says more accountability and he goes to  this conversation about regulation we've  all had this conversation before he says  regulators need to create an oversight  body to talk about transparency and you  know we've spent the last weeks looking  through so much of this research and  there were thousands of pages of  research and by the way we should  mention facebook did this research about  its own company and what he said was you  know there should be a safe way for this  research to go to other researchers and  people to share this so we can all have  a better understanding of what happens  on these social media platforms if  there's a way to do so and respect  people's privacy so i think that's a  place to start and by the way all of  this is important to say that this is  coming at a time where facebook is  reportedly rebranding to be a metaverse  company  and you know you might not have heard  the word metaverse yet but you will and  your children will because this is this  next iteration of the internet and so  we've got to start talking about safety  there yeah wow  it's a lot i wonder if the information  we now have too will impact how we use  our devices right you know now that we  have the information are we going to be  more intentional as a group as humans  and not allowing these devices to  control us lori thank you so much

